2026-11-06T03:19:03.5813690Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-11-06T03:19:03.5823019Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-11-06T03:19:03.5823449Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-11-06T03:19:03.5823761Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-11-06T03:19:03.5823912Z 
2026-11-06T03:19:03.5824038Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-11-06T03:19:03.5824363Z 
2026-11-06T03:19:03.5824506Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-11-06T03:19:03.5824810Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-11-06T03:19:03.5824973Z 
2026-11-06T03:19:03.5825046Z If you would like to
2026-11-06T03:19:03.5825241Z see the output, try like this:
2026-11-06T03:19:03.5825381Z 
2026-11-06T03:19:03.5825518Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-11-06T03:19:03.5825809Z   $ sh ./install-nix
